   "name": "nightly-reviewer",
   "service_account": "autopilot-runs/nightly-reviewer"
  },
  "doc": {
   "description": "Every night, reviews the fleet's catalog, Argo apps and metrics and reports what needs a person.",
   "identity": {
    "serviceAccount": "autopilot-runs/nightly-reviewer",
    "type": "workload"
   },
   "kind": "scheduled",
   "name": "nightly-reviewer",
   "owner": "group:default/team-platform",
   "profile": {
    "compute": "small",
    "limits": {
     "children": 0,
     "githubCalls": 0,
     "modelTokens": 300000,
     "openPrs": 0,
     "toolCalls": 100,
     "ttlMinutes": 30
    },
    "models": [
     "claude-sonnet-5-5"
    ],
    "network": "clearance+model",
    "tierCeiling": "T0",
    "tools": [
     "catalog.read",
     "argo.app.get",
     "metrics.query"
    ]
   },
   "runtime": {
    "framework": "generic",
    "image": "ghcr.io/jfillman/autopilot-agent-runtime@sha256:b1c7b65ba8405726879f27f18982d455cdb4f6c25cdb09eddd642b21e8fbbe6a",
    "instructions": "Review the fleet's apps on hangar-dev for what a person should look at today. Change nothing. 1. catalog.read `kind=component,spec.type=service` (a query without `=` is a full-text search, not a filter). The apps are the results whose system is `app-<name>-cicd`; skip the rest. 2. argo.app.get `<name>-dev` (e.g. boarding-api-dev) for each app: sync and health. 3. metrics.query, all apps at once: `sum by (namespace) (increase(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total{namespace=~\"app-.*-dev\"}[24h]))`; `sum by (namespace) (kube_pod_status_ready{condition=\"false\",namespace=~\"app-.*-dev\"})`; `sum by (service, status_code) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_calls_total{span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\",service=~\".*-dev\"}[24h]))` (STATUS_CODE_ERROR is the error share); p95 `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (service, le) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_latency_bucket{span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\",service=~\".*-dev\"}[24h])))`. An app missing from the traces results had no requests (dev is often idle): say \"no traffic\", not a fault. Report one line per app that needs attention (what and why), then one all-clear line naming the apps checked and fine. If a step fails, say which and why."
   },
   "triggers": [
    {
     "every": "24h",
     "type": "interval"
    }
   ]
  },
  "name": "nightly-reviewer",
  "runs_in": "cluster",
  "scope": {
   "agent_kind": "scheduled",
