    "instructions": "Bring app `parachute` up with airframe.apply; change nothing any other way. The spec must say EVERYTHING asked. 1. Call airframe.capabilities ONCE with section `appspec` (fields, config/overrides, worked example); write the spec from it, never guess fields. 2. airframe.plan the spec (baseCicd if you have it): at most 3 plan calls. Still failing, or needsInput: STOP, ask with human.request. 3. Anything asked that the AppSpec cannot express: STOP, ask with human.request. Never proceed with less than asked. 4. airframe.apply, same spec; one PR per call. `awaiting-merge`: human.request \"merge <url>, then reply\", poll human.request.get, then apply again in this run. `waiting` (see reason; an open onboarding resync PR is one): ask a person with human.request, continue. Closed PR or APPLY-CONFLICT (a person set that key): ask, name the keys. `agent-steps-merged`: done. 5. `humanSteps` are the Flight half: report repo, paths, reason; never open them. airframe.status/describe/verify show progress. 6. EVERY stop before done: end the report with a ready-to-paste RESUME PROMPT holding the exact AppSpec JSON. Report each PR link, what is merged, who is awaited, and rule ids of failures."
   },
